Barlow 400 and 600 and Barlow Condensed 600 and 700, Latin subset, woff2. Source: github.com/google/fonts at commit 2fe1e8c6b137fb13041a7cfca6fdcd8a910ea4dc (2026-11-02), ofl/barlow and ofl/barlowcondensed, which hold the TTFs; the Latin woff2 are made here from them with fontTools 4.68.0 (brotli 1.2.1) and the unicode range Google Fonts' CSS API serves as 'latin'. Licence: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (OFL.txt, the same file in both folders); no Reserved Font Name is declared in it. Inlined as data: URIs in @font-face by scripts/camera_page.py, which checks each woff2 by its sha256 below; loaded from nowhere.

Command, per file (the layout features kept are the subsetter's default plus tabular and lining figures and kerning):
  python -m fontTools.subset SOURCE.ttf --unicodes=U+0000-00FF,U+0131,U+0152-0153,U+02BB-02BC,U+02C6,U+02DA,U+02DC,U+0304,U+0308,U+0329,U+2000-206F,U+20AC,U+2122,U+2191,U+2193,U+2212,U+2215,U+FEFF,U+FFFD --flavor=woff2 --layout-features+=tnum,lnum,pnum,kern --output-file=NAME.woff2

